  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The System Window",
    "overview": "The app is Solo Leveling's System rendered as a premium native Android app. The ground is near-black ink with a violet cast; on it sit quiet solid rows and cards that hold the user's own data, and, rarely, a translucent violet window with a hairline frame and 45° notched corners. That window is reserved for THE SYSTEM: when it speaks (a morning briefing, a status readout, a quest-complete reply), it speaks inside a frame headed by a bracketed, letter-spaced title such as \"[ STATUS ]\". Everything else stays flat and plain so the window keeps its weight.\n\nEach screen does one job. Today answers \"what do I do next\" with one briefing and one quest; Quests lists; Log is a sheet; Arena compares; Status shows who the user is. Secondary content sits behind a row with a chevron, a sheet, or a detail screen. Density is moderate: a 24dp gap between blocks, 64dp rows, 48dp targets. Rewards are cold. Progress arrives as System output (\"+3.3 DISCIPLINE. Logged.\"), never as celebration, and nothing on screen claims more than the data supports.\n\nThe visual rejections confirmed by the owner are generic neon blue and the stacked dashboard, where rank, stats, briefing and quests share one scroll.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ink-black ground, violet-tinted neutrals, a single Monarch violet accent.",
      "System windows for THE SYSTEM's voice only. They are translucent in flow and opaque when they float.",
      "Chakra Petch for display, numbers and labels; Noto Sans for reading.",
      "Four type sizes (12 / 15 / 20) plus one display figure per screen.",
      "Five domain colours that belong to their dot, chip and label only.",
      "Flat surfaces. Depth comes from tone and frame, and the only glow is on the rank emblem."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Pressable Violet Rule",
        "body": "Monarch violet fills only things you can press, plus the one hero highlight. If it is violet and filled, a tap does something.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Domain Owns Its Mark Rule",
        "body": "A domain colour appears as the dot, the caps label or the frame of something scoped to that domain. It never becomes a background.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three-Plus-One Rule",
        "body": "Only 12, 15 and 20 exist, plus one display figure per screen. No other font size and nothing below 12. Letter-spacing comes only from the label role; the nav label's 0.4 tracking is the one exception, and it is owned by the kit.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Android Weight Rule",
        "body": "Weight is chosen by font family name (ChakraPetch_700Bold, NotoSans_600SemiBold), never by `fontWeight`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Solid-When-Floating Rule",
        "body": "A System window in the flow is translucent over the ink. A window that floats over content (the echo, notices) uses the opaque #1A1430 fill, so nothing shows through behind THE SYSTEM's words.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Glow Rule",
        "body": "Glow belongs to the rank emblem. Nothing else is lit.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour from `useColors()` and every type style from `constants/type.ts`. The accent follows the adaptive uiState.",
      "Do give each screen one job. Move secondary content behind a chevron row, a sheet or a detail screen, and keep every feature reachable.",
      "Do put THE SYSTEM's messages, and only those, in a System window with a bracketed caps title. Use the `solid` fill whenever the window floats.",
      "Do answer a completed quest with the [ QUEST COMPLETE ] echo above the tab bar, reporting the amount the server applied.",
      "Do keep rewards cold: state the delta and the domain, then \"Logged.\" Nothing more.",
      "Do label simulated or partial data honestly (\"SIMULATED\", \"Base. Your streak adds more.\", \"new\").",
      "Do make every touch target at least 48dp with Android ripple feedback, keep system Back working, and respect reduce motion.",
      "Do write empty states as one System line plus one primary action."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use generic neon blue or build a stacked dashboard that puts rank, stats, briefing and quests on one scroll.",
      "Don't wrap ordinary data cards in System windows. The frame belongs to THE SYSTEM's voice.",
      "Don't use any font size other than 12, 15, 20 and the single display figure, or any size below 12.",
      "Don't fill surfaces or buttons with a domain colour, or fill anything that cannot be pressed with Monarch violet.",
      "Don't put a small caps eyebrow over a heading. Bracketed window titles and caps labels heading a list are the world's own devices; a kicker above a title is not.",
      "Don't use coloured side borders thicker than 1px, cards nested in cards, gradient text, emoji or unicode glyphs as icons, or glow anywhere except the rank emblem.",
      "Don't show a claim the data does not support (no promotion percentage on day 1, no \"LIVE\" over simulated rivals, no review of seven days before day 7).",
      "Don't use a modal for something that does not need to interrupt."
    ]
  }
}
